    <questiondescription format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p id="author">Godfrey Wabwire</p>
<p id="concept">N/Ap>
<p id="reviewer">Nixson Kiplagat</p>
<p id="reviewer">2</p>
<p id="description">The problem involves determining the limit of a three-variable function as \((x, y, z)\) approaches the point \((a, b, c)\). The function is given by \(px - e^{pyz} \). Substituting the specified values into the expression and simplifying, we need to evaluate the limit numerically. The result will be the value the function approaches as the variables get close to the given point.</p>]]></text>
    </questiondescription>
